  "body": "## What this fixes\n- Cennik/model planning now counts only `FIRST_OFFER + CONFIRMED` rows from `real_action_audit` as newly started negotiations instead of counting every daily quota action (which also included `NEXT_STEP`).\n- Negotiation capacity no longer reserves future slots for an active listing that is already superseded by another *active confirmed* marketplace owner.\n- Keeps stale/terminal-owner cases fail-safe: the planner only ignores a row when another owner is still active, so a sole current conversation is not silently dropped.\n- Adds a regression test for the duplicate-capacity case.\n\n## Why\nThe database audit on 2026-08-31 showed `Galaxy S25` as 6 in the UI while the actual confirmed breakdown was 5 `FIRST_OFFER` + 1 `NEXT_STEP`. It also found legacy cross-bot duplicates that consumed planner capacity before the database cleanup.\n\n## Safety\nThis PR does not loosen the global FIRST_OFFER ownership guard and does not auto-transfer terminal claims. The one-time legacy ownership cleanup was performed separately after a dry-run and protected-history validation.",
